{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p97#2","rows":[{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["لا تدخلوا بيوتا غير بيوتكم"],"type":"reports","speaker":"رجل من الأنصار","stance":"reports","claim":"An Anṣārī man reported that a woman asked how to handle visitors who entered while she was privately undressed; the Prophet told her to send them back, and the verse was revealed.","anchor":"روي : عن عدي بن ثابت عن رجل من الأنصار قال : جاءت امرأة إلى رسول الله عليه السلام","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["بيوتا غير بيوتكم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“Other than your houses” follows the customary case of living in one’s own property; tenants and borrowers also need permission before entering.","anchor":"وصف البيوت بمغايرة بيوتهم خارج مخرج العادة التي هي سكنى كل أحد في ملكه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["حتى تستأنسوا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Istīʾnās here means seeking permission from whoever has authority to grant it.","anchor":"أي تستأذنوا ممن يملك الإذن من أصحابها.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["حتى تستأنسوا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The word can mean inquiry and uncovering someone’s state, or becoming at ease after the fear that permission may be refused.","anchor":"من الاستئناس بمعنى الاستعلام من آنس الشيء إذا أبصره مكشوفا فعلم به","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["حتى تستأنسوا"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The wording is metonymy: it names the ease that follows permission while intending permission itself.","anchor":"فيؤول المعنى إلى أن يؤذن لكم وهو من باب الكناية حيث ذكر الاستئناس اللازم وأريد الإذن الملزوم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["حتى تستأنسوا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي عليه السلام","stance":"reports","claim":"When asked what seeking familiarity means, the Prophet said to say tasbīḥ or takbīr and clear one’s throat to alert the household.","anchor":"وعن النبي عليه السلام في معنى الاستئناس حين سئل عنه فقال : \"هو أن يتكلم الرجل بالتسبيحة والتكبيرة ويتنحنح يؤذن أهل البيت\"","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["لا تدخلوا بيوتا غير بيوتكم"],"type":"law","speaker":"نصاب الاحتساب","stance":"reports","claim":"A cited legal manual permits a wife to enter the homes of her husband’s maḥram relatives without their permission; the author calls this an unusual ruling to verify.","anchor":"قال في \"نصاب الاحتساب\" : امرأة دخلت في بيت غير بغير إذن صاحبه هل يحتسب عليها؟ فالجواب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["لا تدخلوا بيوتا غير بيوتكم"],"type":"law","speaker":"أبو حنيفة رحمه الله","stance":"reports","claim":"The cited ruling says a wife who steals from her husband’s maḥram relatives’ home is not subject to hand amputation according to Abū Ḥanīfa.","anchor":"ولهذا لو سرقت من بيت محارم زوجها لا قطع عليها عند أبي حنيفة رحمه الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["لا تدخلوا بيوتا غير بيوتكم"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In other cases, a woman is subject to the same enforcement of the permission rule as a man.","anchor":"وما في غير ذلك يحتسب عليها كما يحتسب على الرجل لقوله تعالى : {لا تدخلوا بيوتا غير بيوتكم حتى تستأنسوا}","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p98","rows":[{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["وتسلموا على أهلها"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Entering with permission is fine etiquette and a praiseworthy act that brings happiness in both worlds.","anchor":"فالدخول بالإذن من الآداب الجميلة والأفعال المرضية المستتبعة لسعادة الدارين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["وتسلموا على أهلها"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"One should say salām while seeking entry, ask three times, enter and greet again if permitted, and otherwise return.","anchor":"بأن يقول : السلام عليكم أدخل ثلاث مرات فإن أذن له دخل وسلم ثانيا وإلا رجع.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["ذلكم خير لكم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Permission and greeting are better than entering suddenly, even into one’s mother’s home, since she might be unclothed.","anchor":"من أن تدخلوا بغتة ولو على الأم فإنها تحتمل أن تكون عريانة.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["وتسلموا على أهلها"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The rule guides Muslims away from the pre-Islamic habit of greeting a strange household with “good morning” or “good evening” on entry.","anchor":"وفيه إرشاد إلى ترك تحية أهل الجاهلية حين الدخول فإن الرجل منهم كان إذا دخل بيتا غريبا صباحا.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["وتسلموا على أهلها"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الكاشفي","stance":"reports","claim":"Kāshifī advises announcing one’s arrival at home by speaking, calling out, or clearing the throat so residents can cover themselves and prepare.","anchor":"قال الكاشفي : (وكفته اند كسي كه برعيال خود درمي آيد بايدكه بكلمة يا بآ وازيا بتنحنحى اعلام كند","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["لعلكم تذكرون"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“So that you may remember” depends on an omitted clause: the command was given so people would remember, take heed, and act accordingly.","anchor":"متعلق بمضمر أي أمرتم به كي تذكروا وتتعظوا وتعلموا بموجبه.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["وتسلموا على أهلها"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Salām is a Muslim sunnah and the greeting of Paradise; it produces affection and removes resentment and rancor.","anchor":"اعلم أن السلام من سنة المسلمين وهو تحية أهل الجنة ومجلبة للمودة وناف للحقد والضغينة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["وتسلموا على أهلها"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي عليه السلام","stance":"reports","claim":"A report says Adam sneezed, praised God, received God’s blessing, then greeted the assembled angels; God identified this as his greeting and his descendants’ greeting.","anchor":"روي : عنه عليه السلام قال : \"لما خلق الله تعالى آدم ونفخ فيه الروح عطس فقال : الحمدفقال الله تعالى يرحمك ربك يا آدم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["وتسلموا على أهلها"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي عليه السلام","stance":"reports","claim":"A report lists six Muslim duties: greet on meeting, answer an invitation, counsel in absence, bless after a sneeze, visit the sick, and attend the funeral.","anchor":"وروي عنه عليه السلام قال : \"حق المسلم على المسلم ست يسلم عليه إذا لقيه ويجيبه إذا دعاه وينصح له بالغيب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["لا تدخلوا بيوتا غير بيوتكم"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In emergencies such as fire, theft, unlawful killing, or an apparent wrong requiring removal, permission and greeting are not required; necessity suspends prohibitions.","anchor":"فحينئذ لا يجب الاستئذان والتسليم فإن كل ذلك مستثنى بالدليل وهو ما قاله الفقهاء من أن مواقع الضرورات مستثناة من قواعد الشرع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["24:27"],"words":["حتى تستأنسوا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الكشاف","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kashshāf laments that people have abandoned many religious practices as if they were abrogated, including seeking permission.","anchor":"قال صاحب \"الكشاف\" : وكم من باب من أبواب الدين هو عند الناس كالشريعة المنسوخة قد تركوا العمل بها وباب الاستئذان من ذلك","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p156#3","rows":[{"verses":["25:41"],"words":["وإذا رأوك"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“When they see you” addresses Muḥammad and identifies the mockers as Quraysh.","anchor":"أي : أبصروك يا محمد يعني قريشا.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:41"],"words":["إن يتخذونك إلا هزوا"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The particle in the exception is negating: they do nothing but make the Prophet an object of mockery.","anchor":"إن نافية أي ما يتخذونك إلا موضع هزو أي يستهزئون بك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:41"],"words":["إن يتخذونك إلا هزوا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Their mockery was contemptuous and taunting, not merely a refusal to believe or the production of false doubts.","anchor":"إن نافية أي ما يتخذونك إلا موضع هزو أي يستهزئون بك قائلين بطريق الاستحقار والتهكم.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:41"],"words":["أهذا الذى بعث الله رسولا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"They ask whether this is the messenger God sent to establish the proof against them.","anchor":"أي : بعث الله إلينا رسولا ليثبت الحجة علينا.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:41"],"words":["أهذا الذى بعث الله رسولا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو جهل","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Jahl reportedly said to Abū Sufyān, “This is the prophet of Banū ʿAbd Manāf,” as an expression of contempt.","anchor":"وهو قول أبي جهل لأبي سفيان وهذا نبي بني عبد مناف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:41"],"words":["وإذا رأوك"],"type":"inward","speaker":"التأويلات النجمية","stance":"reports","claim":"The Najmiyya reading says sensory people cannot perceive prophecy through outward sight; it is recognized by insight illuminated by God, which they lack.","anchor":"وفي \"التأويلات النجمية\" : يشير إلى أن أهل الحس لا يرون النبوة والرسالة بالحس الظاهر لأنها تدرك بنظر البصيرة بنور الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:41"],"words":["أهذا الذى بعث الله رسولا"],"type":"inward","speaker":"التأويلات النجمية","stance":"reports","claim":"Because they cannot understand prophetic speech, they mock the messenger as a human being who needs food and drink.","anchor":"فلما سمعوا منه ما لم يهتدوا به من كلام النبوة والرسالة ما اتخذوه إلا هزؤا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:41"],"words":["أهذا الذى بعث الله رسولا"],"type":"links","speaker":"المثنوي","stance":"reports","claim":"The cited Mathnawī verses illustrate that outward resemblance conceals profound differences, as between a written lion and a real one, or honey and dung.","anchor":"وفي \"المثنوي\" : كارا كان را قياس ازخود مكير كره ماند درنبشتن شير شير","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p157#2","rows":[{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["أرأيت"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“Have you seen?” can introduce information or a question; here it expresses astonishment.","anchor":"كلمة أرأيت تستعمل تارة للإعلام وتارة للسؤال وههنا للتعجيب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["*"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The second object, “his god,” precedes the first for emphasis because it is the focus of the astonishment.","anchor":"وإلهه مفعولة ثان قدم على الأول للاعتناء به لأنه الذي يدور عليه أمر التعجب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["*"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hawāʾ first meant what one loves or desires, then the desired object; usage came to associate it especially with blameworthy desire.","anchor":"والهوى مصدر هويه إذا أحبه واشتهاه ثم سمي به المهوى المشتهى محمودا كان أو مذموما ثم غلب على غير المحمود","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["*"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hawāʾ is what temperament inclines toward and the soul craves merely from desire, without transmitted authority or rational proof.","anchor":"فالهوى ما يميل إليه الطبع وتهواه النفس بمجرد الاشتهاء من غير سند منقول ودليل معقول.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["*"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A person makes desire a god by obeying it and building religion on it while rejecting all proof; the question calls for astonishment.","anchor":"والمعنى أرأيت يا محمد من جعل هواه إلها لنفسه بأن أطاعه وبنى عليه أمر دينه معرضا عن استماع الحجة والبرهان بالكلية","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A Persian anecdote says some Arabs worshipped stones they found attractive, discarding an old idol when they found a better one; it names Ḥārith ibn Qays among them.","anchor":"(وكفته أند قومي بودند ازعرب كه سنك مي رستيدند هركاهكه ايشانرا سنكي نيكو بجشم آمدي ودل ايشان آن خواستي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي عليه السلام","stance":"reports","claim":"A hadith states that no deity is more hateful to God than desire.","anchor":"وفي الحديث : \"ما عبد إله أبغض على الله من الهوى\"","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["*"],"type":"inward","speaker":"التأويلات النجمية","stance":"reports","claim":"The Najmiyya reading says whoever loves something other than God and becomes occupied with it is worshipping his own desire, which prefers that object to God.","anchor":"فهو عابد هواه كما في \"التأويلات النجمية\".","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["*"],"type":"inward","speaker":"سيد حسني رحمه الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Sayyid Ḥasanī’s Tarab al-majālis traces human desire to the union of Iblīs and the world, whose effects produce rejected customs and diverse religions.","anchor":"سيد حسني رحمه الله در طرب المجالس أورده كه ون آدم صفي عليه السلام باحوا عقد بستند إبليس ودنيا بيكديكر يوستند","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p157#3","rows":[{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["أرأيت من اتخذ إلهه هواه"],"type":"inward","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The saying “desire was the first god worshipped on earth” makes false deities branches of desire; resisting desire leads to true faith.","anchor":"الهوى أول إله عبد في الأرض في شأنه وارد شده وزبان القرآن في حقه فرموده","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["من اتخذ إلهه هواه"],"type":"inward","speaker":"أبو سليمان رحمه الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Sulaymān says following desire kills the self: remembrance is its life, heedlessness its death, and heedlessness leads to passions and the state of the dead.","anchor":"قال أبو سليمان رحمه الله من أتبع نفسه هواها فقد سعى في قتلها لأن حياتها بالذكر وموتها وقتلها بالغفلة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["هواه"],"type":"inward","speaker":"المثنوي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Mathnawī contrasts prophets and unbelievers in the same worldly marketplace: lust traps both, but believers are genuine gold and unbelievers counterfeit.","anchor":"وفي المثنوي اين جهان شهوتي يتخانة ايست انبيا وكافرانرا لأنه ايست ليك شهوت بندة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["هواه"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أكابر","stance":"reports","claim":"An interpretation attributed to elders says dreaming that the Prophet has died signifies weakness or deficiency in the dreamer’s religious practice; losing divine presence is analogous.","anchor":"أكابر گفته اندكه اكر كسي درخواب بيندكه يغمبر صلى الله عليه وسلم مرده است تعبيرش آنست كه درشريعت اين صاحب واقعة قصوري وفتوري واقع شده است","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["هواه"],"type":"inward","speaker":"جامي رحمه الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Jāmī offers another reading: the dreamed-of “god” is a desire the person had worshipped; its disappearance from the heart signals increased presence with God.","anchor":"مولانا نور الدين عبد الرحمن جامي رحمه الله اين سخن را تأويل ديكر كرده بودند فرموده كه ميتواند بودكه بحكم آيت كريمة أرءيت من اتخذ إلاهه هوااه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["عليه"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“Against him” refers to the person who has made his desire a god; wakīl means a guardian protecting him from idolatry and sins.","anchor":"عليه برآنكس كه هواي خودرا خدا ساخته وكيلا حفيظا تمنعه عن الشرك والمعاصي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["أفأنت تكون عليه وكيلا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The question denies that the Prophet is charged with guarding such a person; his task is warning, not being his keeper.","anchor":"لست موكلا على حفظه بل أنت منذر فهذا الاستفهام للإنكار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["25:43"],"words":["أفأنت تكون عليه وكيلا"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The rhetorical denial does not forbid calling them; it tells the Prophet he has completed warning and removing excuses.","anchor":"وليس هذا نهيا عن دعائه إياهم بل الإعلام بأنه قد قضى ما عليه من الإنذار والأعذار","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p191#2","rows":[{"verses":["26:6"],"words":["فسيأتيهم"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The future threat is certain; the causal fa links it to their turning away, which leads to denial and then mockery.","anchor":"البتة من غير تخلف أصلا والفاء للسببية ، أي لسبب إعراضهم المؤدي إلى التكذيب المؤدي إلى الاستهزاء.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:6"],"words":["*"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The news they mocked is of near and later punishments; seeing them will establish whether the Qur’an deserved belief and honor or rejection.","anchor":"أخبار الذكر الذي كانوا يستهزؤون به من العقوبات العاجلة والآجلة التي بمشاهدتها يقفون على حقيقة حال القرآن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:6"],"words":["أنباء"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A nabaʾ is grave, consequential news, which heightens the warning.","anchor":"وفيه تهويل له لأن النبأ لا يطلق إلا على خبر خطير له وقع عظيم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:6"],"words":["*"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الكاشفي","stance":"reports","claim":"Kāshifī warns that regret after the consequences of denial appear cannot help; learning too late what benefits one is useless.","anchor":"قال الكاشفي : (وبعد از ظهور نتايج تكذيب شيماني نفع ندهد امروز بدان مصلحت خويش كه فردا داني وشيمان شوى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["أولم يروا"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The interrogative hamza rebukes; the conjunction links to an omitted thought: did Quraysh reject and mock without looking at the signs?","anchor":"الهمزة للإنكار التوبيخي والواو للعطف على مقدر يقتضيه المقام أي أفعل المكذبون من قريش ما فعلوا من الإعراض","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p191#3","rows":[{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["إلى الأرض"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The earth’s marvels should deter the rejecters from their conduct and invite them to what they have turned away from.","anchor":"أي إلى عجائبها الزاجرة عما فعلوا الداعية إلى الإقبال إلى ما أعرضوا.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["كم أنبتنا فيها من كل زوج كريم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God grew abundant pleasing, beneficial kinds of plants, including fragrant flowers, colorful blossoms, varied leaves, and food for people and animals.","anchor":"من كل صنف مرضي كثير المنافع أنبتنا فيها وتخصيص النبات النافع بالذكر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["كم أنبتنا فيها من كل زوج كريم"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"أهل التفسير","stance":"reports","claim":"Exegetes parse kam as an accusative exclamatory quantifier of abundance, with min kull zawj as its specification; kull marks comprehensiveness.","anchor":"قال أهل التفسير : كم خبرية منصوبة بما بعدها على المفعولية والجمع بينها وبين كل لأن كل للإحاطة بجميع أزواج النبات","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["من كل زوج كريم"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Kull means every kind; karīm means praiseworthy and commendable, as in a pleasing face, useful book, or brave man.","anchor":"والكريم من كل شيء مرضيه ومحموده يقال وجه كريم أي مرضي في حسنه وجماله وكتاب كريم مرضي في معانيه وفوائده","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["من كل زوج كريم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Useful plants are singled out because they display both divine power and blessing, although even harmful plants carry wisdom and benefit.","anchor":"وتخصيص النبات النافع بالذكر دون ما عداه من أصناف الضار وإن كان كل نبت متضمنا لفائدة وحكمة لاختصاصه بالدلالة على القدرة والنعمة معا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["من كل زوج كريم"],"type":"inward","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"As the outward earth grows noble plants, God grows faith, trust, certainty, sincerity, and fine character in the hearts of gnostics.","anchor":"كما أنبت من أرض الظاهر كل صنف ونوع من النبات الحسن الكريم كذلك أنبت في أرض قلوب العارفين كل نبت من الإيمان والتوكل واليقين والإخلاص","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["من كل زوج كريم"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي عليه السلام","stance":"reports","claim":"A Prophetic report compares the growth of faith in the heart to the growth of vegetation.","anchor":"كما قال عليه السلام : \"لا إله إلا الله ينبت الإيمان كما ينبت البقل\"","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["من كل زوج كريم"],"type":"inward","speaker":"أبو بكر بن طاهر","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Ṭāhir calls Adam and Eve the noblest earthly plant-pair because they occasioned the appearance of messengers, prophets, saints, and gnostics.","anchor":"قال أبو بكر بن طاهر : أكرم زوج من نبات الأرض آدم وحواء فإنهما كانا سببا في إظهار الرسل والأنبياء والأولياء والعارفين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:7"],"words":["من كل زوج كريم"],"type":"inward","speaker":"الشعبي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Shaʿbī compares people to plants of the earth: those who enter Paradise are noble, and those who enter Hell are base.","anchor":"قال الشعبي : الناس من نبات الأرض فمن دخل الجنة فهو كريم ومن دخل النار فهو لئيم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:8"],"words":["إن في ذلك"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“In that” may refer to the growth just described as a whole or to each of the plant varieties.","anchor":"أي : في الإنبات المذكور أو في كل واحد من تلك الأصناف.","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p192#2","rows":[{"verses":["26:10"],"words":["وإذ نادى ربك موسى"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The temporal clause is governed by an implied “remember.”","anchor":"إذ منصوب باذكر المقدر والمناداة والنداء رفع الصوت","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:10"],"words":["نادى"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Munādāt means raising the voice; the root evokes moisture, associated with eloquence because a moist mouth produces beautiful speech.","anchor":"والمناداة والنداء رفع الصوت وأصله من الندى وهو الرطوبة واستعارته للصوت","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:10"],"words":["وإذ نادى ربك موسى"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Muḥammad is told to recall for his people God’s call to Moses by the burning tree when he returned from Midian, and to warn them of Pharaoh’s people’s fate.","anchor":"والمعنى اذكر يا محمد لقومك وقت نداءه تعالى وكلامه موسى أي ليلة رأى الشجرة والنار حين رجع من مدين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:10"],"words":["أن ائت القوم الظالمين"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The clause beginning an is explanatory after “called,” meaning “that is,” and ītiyān means coming easily.","anchor":"تفسير نادى فإن مفسرة بمعنى أي والإتيان مجيء بسهولة.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:10"],"words":["القوم الظالمين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The people wronged themselves through disbelief and sins, enslaved the Israelites, and slaughtered their sons.","anchor":"أنفسهم بالكفر والمعاصي واستعباد بني إسرائيل وذبح أبنائهم.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:11"],"words":["قوم فرعون"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“The people of Pharaoh” is appositional to “the people”; naming the people alone signals Pharaoh’s prominence among those judged.","anchor":"بدل من القوم والاقتصار على القوم للإيذان بشهرة أن فرعون أول داخل في الحكم.","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p192#3","rows":[{"verses":["26:11"],"words":["ألا يتقون"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The clause is a new sentence with no syntactic attachment; alā is an exhortation to act.","anchor":"استئناف لا محل له من الإعراب وألا تحضيض على الفعل أتبعه إرساله إليهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:11"],"words":["ألا يتقون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Moses is sent to warn them, expressing astonishment at their injustice and aggression: will they not fear God and avert punishment through faith and obedience?","anchor":"أتبعه إرساله إليهم لإنذار وتعجيبا من غلوهم في الظلم وإفراطهم في العدوان أي ألا يخافون الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:12"],"words":["قال"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“He said” begins the response to the implied question of what Moses said; he speaks in supplication to God.","anchor":"استئناف كأنه قيل : فماذا قال موسى؟ فقيل : قال متضرعا إلى الله تعالى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:12"],"words":["رب"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Rabb is glossed in Persian as “my sustainer.”","anchor":"قال متضرعا إلى الله تعالى : {رب} (أي روردكار من).","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:12"],"words":["إني أخاف"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Fear is expecting harm on the basis of a probable or certain indication; hope and desire similarly anticipate a good outcome.","anchor":"الخوف توقع مكروه عن إمارة مظنونة أو معلومة كما أن الرجاء والطمع توقع محبوب عن أمارة مظنونة أو معلومة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:12"],"words":["أن يكذبون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Moses fears that they will immediately deny his prophethood and what he says.","anchor":"ينكروا نبوتي وما أقول من أول الأمر.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:12"],"words":["إني أخاف أن يكذبون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"بعض الكبار","stance":"reports","claim":"Some spiritual masters say Moses feared for the people out of compassion; grammatically, the yāʾ of yakdhibūnī is omitted because the kasra suffices.","anchor":"قال بعض الكبار : خوفه كان شفقة عليهم وأصله يكذبوني فحذفت الياء استغناء بالكسر.","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p211#3","rows":[{"verses":["26:105"],"words":["كذبت"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The perfect verb conveys continuing denial from the beginning of Noah’s preaching through its end.","anchor":"تكذيبا مستمرا من حين الدعوة إلى انتهائها.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:105"],"words":["قوم نوح"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qawm can mean a group including men and women, or men specifically with women included by subordination; its feminine diminutive is qūwayma.","anchor":"القوم الجماعة من الرجال والنساء معا أو الرجال خاصة وتدخل النساء على التبعية ويؤنث بدليل مجيء تصغيره على قويمة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:105"],"words":["المرسلين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“The messengers” means Noah alone, while the plural reflects that denying one messenger denies all who share tawḥīd and basic law, or because each messenger commands belief in all.","anchor":"أي : نوحا وحده والجمع باعتبار أن من كذب رسولا واحدا فقد كذب الجميع لاجتماع الكل على التوحيد وأصول الشرائع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:106"],"words":["إذ قال لهم"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The temporal clause describes the extended period of denial and the events between both sides until the matter ended.","anchor":"ظرف للتكذيب على أنه عبارة عن زمان مديد وقع فيه ما وقع من الجانبين إلى تمام الأمر.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:106"],"words":["أخوهم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah is called their brother by lineage so they would know his truthfulness and faithfulness, and recognize his language, making acceptance easier.","anchor":"في النسب لئلا يجهل أمره في الصدق والديانة ولتعرف لغته فيؤدي ذلك إلى القبول.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:106"],"words":["نوح"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“Noah” is an explanatory apposition clarifying “their brother.”","anchor":"{نوح} عطف بيان لأخوهم. {ألا تتقون} الله حيث تعبدون غيره","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:106"],"words":["ألا تتقون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah urges them to fear God because they worship others besides Him.","anchor":"الله حيث تعبدون غيره. وبالفارسية (أيا منمي ترسيد از خداي تعالى كه ترك عبادت أو ميكنيد)","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p211#4","rows":[{"verses":["26:107"],"words":["إني لكم رسول"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah’s apostleship is from God.","anchor":"{إني لكم رسول} من جهته تعالى.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:107"],"words":["أمين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah was publicly known as trustworthy; one trustworthy in worldly matters is trustworthy in revelation and the message.","anchor":"مشهور بالأمانة فيما بينكم ومن كان أمينا على أمور الدنيا كان أمينا على الوحي والرسالة.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:108"],"words":["فاتقوا الله وأطيعون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah calls them to fear God and obey him in monotheism and obedience, since he will neither betray nor harm them; the fa follows from his trustworthiness.","anchor":"فإني لا أخونكم ولا أريدكم بسوء والفاء لترتيب ما بعدها على الأمانة.","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p211#5","rows":[{"verses":["26:108"],"words":["فاتقوا الله وأطيعون"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The repeated command follows from Noah’s lack of greed; repetition emphasizes that trustworthiness and refusal of payment each independently require obedience.","anchor":"الفاء لترتيب ما بعدها على تنزهه عن الطمع والتكرير للتأكيد والتنبيه على أن كلا من الأمانة وقطع الطمع مستقل في إيجاب التقوى والطاعة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:111"],"words":["أنؤمن لك"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah’s people use a rhetorical question to deny that they will believe him.","anchor":"{قالوا} أي : قوم نوح {أنؤمن لك} الاستفهام للإنكار ، أي لا نؤمن لك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:111"],"words":["واتبعك الأرذلون"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"They call his followers the lowliest in social standing, wealth, and status, likening them to disreputable people whose company they reject.","anchor":"أي والحال قد أتبعك الأقلون جاها ومالا أي وهذه حالك كما تقول لا نصحبك وصحبك السفلة.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:111"],"words":["الأرذلون"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-arḏalūn is the plural of al-arḏal, denoting baseness, low worth, and someone rejected for inferiority.","anchor":"والأرذلون جمع الأرذل والرذالة الخسة والدناءة والرذال المرغوب عنه لرداءته","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:111"],"words":["واتبعك الأرذلون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Their argument shows shallow judgment: they prize worldly wealth, though worldly goods weigh nothing with God and true nobility is winning the afterlife.","anchor":"وهذا من كمال سخافة عقولهم وقصرهم أنظارهم على الدنيا وكون الأشرف عندهم من هو أكثر منها حظا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:111"],"words":["واتبعك الأرذلون"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Quraysh said the same of the Prophet’s companions; prophets and saints are often followed by the poor, who inherit their call, knowledge, experience, and trials.","anchor":"وهكذا كانت قريش تقول في أصحاب رسول الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:111"],"words":["واتبعك الأرذلون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The reality of the spiritual path rarely comes to people of rank and wealth.","anchor":"وذلك لأن الحقيقة من أرباب الجاه والثروة لم تأت إلا نادرا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:111"],"words":["الأرذلون"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The cited Persian couplet reinforces that true greatness is spiritual rather than a matter of worldly stature.","anchor":"ذران سرست بزركي ه نيست فكربزكي","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p212#2","rows":[{"verses":["26:114"],"words":["وما أنا بطارد المؤمنين"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ṭard means driving away, alienating, or expelling someone.","anchor":"الطرد الإزعاج والإبعاد على سبيل الاستخلاف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:114"],"words":["وما أنا بطارد المؤمنين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah answers the implication that he should expel his followers, which the people had made a condition of believing him.","anchor":"وهو جواب عما أوهمه كلامهم أنؤمن لك من استدعاء طردهم وتعليق إيمانهم بذلك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:114"],"words":["وما أنا بطارد المؤمنين"],"type":"inward","speaker":"ابن عطاء رحمه الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAṭāʾ reads this as Noah refusing to turn away anyone who has turned toward his Lord.","anchor":"قال ابن عطاء رحمه الله : وما أنا بمعرض عمن أقبل على ربه.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:115"],"words":["إن أنا إلا نذير مبين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah is only a clear warner to accountable people, whether elite or poor; expelling the poor to attract the rich would contradict his mission.","anchor":"أي ما أنا إلا رسول مبعوث لإنذار المكلفين وزجرهم عن الكفر والمعاصي سواء كانوا من الأعزاء أو الأذلاء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:116"],"words":["*"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Noah’s people threaten him unless he stops preaching and warning.","anchor":"عما تقول يعني عن الدعوة والإنذار.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:116"],"words":["*"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Intihāʾ means to stop or desist.","anchor":"عما تقول يعني عن الدعوة والإنذار.\nوالانتهاء (بازاستيدن).","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:116"],"words":["لتكونن من المرجومين"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الراغب","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Rāghib says rajam is throwing stones, and construes the threat as a promise to kill Noah in the ugliest manner.","anchor":"قال الراغب في \"المفردات\" : الرجام الحجارة والرجم الرمي بالرجام يقال : رجم فهو مرجوم","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p213#3","rows":[{"verses":["26:124"],"words":["إذ قال لهم أخوهم"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The phrase “when their brother said to them” is a temporal clause attached to the account of denial; brotherhood is by lineage.","anchor":"{إذ قال لهم أخوهم} في النسب ظرف للتكذيب.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:124"],"words":["هود"],"type":"reports","speaker":"بعضهم","stance":"reports","claim":"Some say Hūd’s original name was ʿĀbir, he was called Hūd for dignity and calmness, lived 150 years, and was sent to ʿĀd at forty.","anchor":"قال بعضهم : كان اسم هود عابرا وسمي هودا لوقاره وسكونه عاش مائة وخمسين سنة أرسل إلى أورد عاد حين بلغ الأربعين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:124"],"words":["ألا تتقون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hūd asks whether they will not fear God and stop their conduct, especially associating partners and risking divine punishment.","anchor":"الله تعالى فتفعلون ما تفعلون : وبالفارسية (آيا رهيز نميكنيد از شرك واز عقاب إلهي خائف نمي شويد).","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:125"],"words":["إني لكم رسول"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hūd declares that he is a messenger sent by God and publicly known among them for trustworthiness.","anchor":"من جهته تعالى {أمين} مشهور بالأمانة فيما بينكم.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:126"],"words":["فاتقوا الله وأطيعون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"He calls them to fear punishment and obey him in the truth he commands.","anchor":"خافوا من عقابه {وأطيعون} فيما آمركم به من الحق.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:127"],"words":["وما أسألكم عليه من أجر"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hūd asks no wage for delivering the message, unlike some transmitters of stories who seek payment; his reward is from the Lord who sent him.","anchor":"أي : على أداء الرسالة {من أجر} كما يسأل بعض نقلة القصص","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:127"],"words":["إن أجري إلا على رب العالمين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This shows Hūd’s freedom from low ambitions and worldly advantage.","anchor":"وهو بيان لتنزهه عن المطامع الدنية والأعراض الدنيوية","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:127"],"words":["وما أسألكم عليه من أجر"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Ḥāfiẓ’s verse says not to serve for wages, since the beloved knows how to reward the servant who serves.","anchor":"وهو بيان لتنزهه عن المطامع الدنية والأعراض الدنيوية قال الحافظ","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p216","rows":[{"verses":["26:141"],"words":["كذبت ثمود"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The verb is feminine because Thamūd is treated as the tribe; the name comes from their ancestor Thamūd ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿAwṣ ibn ʿĀd ibn Iram ibn Sām ibn Noah.","anchor":"{كذبت ثمود} أنث باعتبار القبيلة وهو اسم جدهم الأعلى وهو ثمود بن عبيد بن عوص بن عاد بن أرم بن سام بن نوح","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:141"],"words":["المرسلين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“The messengers” can mean Ṣāliḥ and earlier messengers, or Ṣāliḥ alone, since rejecting one messenger amounts to rejecting all who share core teachings.","anchor":"يعني : صالحا ومن قبله من المرسلين أو إياه وحده والجمع باعتبار أن تكذيب واحد من الرسل في حكم تكذيب الجميع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:142"],"words":["إذ قال لهم أخوهم"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The temporal clause gives the extended period of denial; “their brother” is by lineage, not religion.","anchor":"ثم بين الوقت الممتد للتكذيب المستمر فقال : {إذ قال لهم أخوهم} النسبي لا الديني فإن الأنبياء محفوظون قبل النبوة معصومون بعدها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:142"],"words":["أخوهم"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The lineage term does not compromise prophetic protection: prophets are preserved before their mission and infallible afterward.","anchor":"فإن الأنبياء محفوظون قبل النبوة معصومون بعدها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:142"],"words":["أخوهم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Calling Ṣāliḥ their brother lets them know his trustworthiness and language, helping them understand and believe his message.","anchor":"وفائدة كونه منهم أن تعرف أمانته ولغته فيؤدي ذلك إلى فهم ما جاء به وتصديقه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:142"],"words":["صالح"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ṣāliḥ is identified as the son of ʿUbayd ibn Āṣif ibn Kāshiḥ ibn Ḥāḏir ibn Thamūd.","anchor":"{صالح} ابن عبيد بن آسف بن كاشح بن حاذر بن ثمود","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:142"],"words":["ألا تتقون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ṣāliḥ asks whether they fear God’s punishment for associating partners with Him.","anchor":"{ألا تتقون} (أيا نمي ترسيد از عذاب خداي كه بدو شرك مي آريد)","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p216#2","rows":[{"verses":["26:143"],"words":["إني لكم رسول أمين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ṣāliḥ’s publicly known trustworthiness obliges them to fear God and obey his call.","anchor":"فإن شهرتي فيما بينكم بالأمانة موجبة لتقوى الله وإطاعتي فيما أدعوكم إليه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:144"],"words":["فاتقوا الله وأطيعون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"He asks no wage for counsel and invitation because payment would cast suspicion on people of integrity.","anchor":"أي : على النصح والدعاء. {من أجر} فإن ذلك تهمة لأهل العفة.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:145"],"words":["إن أجري إلا على رب العالمين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ṣāliḥ’s reward rests with the Lord who sent him, who also rewards His sincere servants.","anchor":"فإنه الذي أرسلني فالأجر عليه بل هو الآجر لعباده الخلص لقوله في الحديث القدسي :","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:145"],"words":["إن أجري إلا على رب العالمين"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي عليه السلام","stance":"reports","claim":"A qudsī hadith says, “Whoever kills him, I am his indemnity,” presenting God as the recompense.","anchor":"لقوله في الحديث القدسي : \"من قتله فأنا ديته\"","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:145"],"words":["إن أجري إلا على رب العالمين"],"type":"links","speaker":"المثنوي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Mathnawī says that for lovers, God is their joy and grief, and He Himself is the wage and fee for their service.","anchor":"وفي \"المثنوي\" : عاشقانرا شادماني وغم أوست دست مزد وأجرت خدمت هم أوست","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:146"],"words":["أتتركون"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The interrogative rebukes them for imagining they will be left without recompense or punishment.","anchor":"{أتتركون} الاستفهام للإنكار والتوبيخ أي أتظنون أنكم تتركون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:146"],"words":["في ما هاهنا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“What is here” means worldly pleasures, with the implication that they assume no afterlife exists.","anchor":"أي : في النعيم الذي هو ثابت في هذا المكان أي الدنيا وأن لا دار للمجازاة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:146"],"words":["آمنين"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Āminīn is circumstantial from the subject of “are you left,” meaning safe from calamities and loss.","anchor":"حال من فاعل تتركون : يعني","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p218#3","rows":[{"verses":["26:160"],"words":["قوم لوط"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The people of Lot are the inhabitants of Sodom and its surrounding settlements.","anchor":"{كذبت قوم لوط} يعني أهل سدوم وما يتبعها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:160"],"words":["المرسلين"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"“The messengers” refers to Lot, Abraham, and those who preceded them.","anchor":"{المرسلين} يعني لوطا وإبراهيم ومن تقدمهما","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:161"],"words":["أخوهم لوط"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Kāshifī says “their brother” means compassionate kinship, since Lot was an outsider, not their blood relative.","anchor":"وذلك لأن لوطا ليس من نسبهم وكان أجنبيا منهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:161"],"words":["أخوهم لوط"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Lot migrated with his paternal uncle Abraham to Syria; Abraham settled him in Jordan, where God sent him to Sodom; Lot was Hārān’s son, and Hārān was Tarikh’s brother.","anchor":"فأنزله إبراهيم الأردن فأرسله الله إلى أهل سدوم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:161"],"words":["ألا تتقون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Lot urges them to fear God’s punishment for idolatry and sins.","anchor":"{ألا تتقون} ألا تخافون من عقاب الله تعالى على الشرك والمعاصي.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:162"],"words":["إني لكم رسول أمين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Lot says he is a messenger from God, publicly known as trustworthy and reliable to everyone.","anchor":"{إني لكم رسول} مرسل من جانب الحق {أمين} مشهور بالأمانة ثقة عند كل أحد.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:163"],"words":["فاتقوا الله وأطيعون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"He commands obedience because the word of a trusted person is reliable.","anchor":"{فاتقوا الله وأطيعون} فإن قول المؤتمن معتمد.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:164"],"words":["وما أسألكم عليه من أجر"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Lot asks no worldly payment for conveying and teaching; seeking it would cast suspicion on the messenger.","anchor":"{ومآ أسالكم عليه} أي : على التبليغ والتعليم {من أجر} جعل ومكافأة دنيوية فإن ذلك تهمة لمن يبلغ عن الله.","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p219","rows":[{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["وتذرون"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Tadharūn means to leave or discard something because one has little regard for it; the verb has no attested perfect form.","anchor":"{وتذرون} تتركون يقال فلان يذر الشيء أي يقذفه لقلة إعداده به ولم يستعمل ماضيه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["ما خلق لكم ربكم من أزواجكم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God created wives for enjoyment; min can denote the female kind generally, or partitive reference to the lawful organ, implying that they also practiced anal intercourse with their wives.","anchor":"{ما خلق لكم ربكم} لأجل استمتاعكم {من أزواجكم} ومن لبيان أن ما أريد به جنس الإناث وللتبعيض إن أريد به العضو المباح منهن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["ما خلق لكم ربكم من أزواجكم"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The partitive reading makes the verse evidence that anal intercourse with wives and enslaved women is forbidden.","anchor":"فتكون الآية دليلا على حرمة أدبار الزوجات والمملوكات","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["ما خلق لكم ربكم من أزواجكم"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي عليه السلام","stance":"reports","claim":"A hadith says that whoever has intercourse with a woman in her anus is disavowed from what was revealed to Muḥammad and will not be looked upon by God.","anchor":"وفي الحديث : \"من أتى امرأة في دبرها فهو بريء مما أنزل على محمد ولا ينظر الله إليه\"","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["بل أنتم قوم عادون"],"type":"reports","speaker":"بعض الصحابة","stance":"reports","claim":"Some Companions declared that the offender had committed disbelief.","anchor":"وقال بعض الصحابة : قد كفر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["بل أنتم قوم عادون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"They are people who overstep the limits in all sins, including this one.","anchor":"{بل أنتم قوم عادون} متجاوزون الحد في جميع المعاصي وهذا من جملتها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["ما خلق لكم ربكم من أزواجكم"],"type":"law","speaker":"أبو حنيفة","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Ḥanīfa rules that male same-sex intercourse warrants discretionary taʿzīr but no fixed ḥadd, contrary to his two disciples.","anchor":"في اللوطي فقال أبو حنيفة : يعزر ولا حد عليه خلافا لصاحبيه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["ما خلق لكم ربكم من أزواجكم"],"type":"law","speaker":"مالك","stance":"reports","claim":"Mālik requires stoning for both participants in male same-sex intercourse, whether married or unmarried.","anchor":"وقال مالك : يجب على الفاعل والمفعول به الرجم أحصنا أو لم يحصنا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:166"],"words":["ما خلق لكم ربكم من أزواجكم"],"type":"law","speaker":"الشافعي وأحمد","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Shāfiʿī and Aḥmad apply the legal rule for fornication to male same-sex intercourse.","anchor":"وعند الشافعي وأحمد حكمه حكم الزنى.","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"BURSEVI:v6p219#2","rows":[{"verses":["26:167"],"words":["*"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Lot’s people threaten him to stop condemning and denouncing their conduct.","anchor":"أي : عن تقبيح أمرنا وإنكارك علينا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:167"],"words":["لتكونن من المخرجين"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"They threaten to expel him from the town violently and disgracefully, as one marked for exile.","anchor":"{لتكونن من المخرجين} من المعهودين بالنفي والإخراج من القرية على عنف وسوء حال.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:168"],"words":["إني لعملكم من القالين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Lot says he intensely detests their act of intercourse with men and will persist in condemning it; his revulsion also shows he wants release from their bad company.","anchor":"من المبغضين أشد البغض كأنه يقلي الفؤاد والكبد لشدته","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:168"],"words":["من القالين"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qālīn is an active participle from qalā, intense hatred, likened to roasting the heart and liver.","anchor":"وهو اسم فاعل من القلي وهو البغض الشديد متعلق بمحذوف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:168"],"words":["لعملكم"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The predicate is elided and min al-qālīn describes it; attaching “your deed” to qālīn as the predicate would put a relative phrase before its antecedent.","anchor":"ولو جعل من القالين خبر إن لعمل القالين في لعملكم فيفضي إلى تقديم الصلة على الموصول","mentions":[]},{"verses":["26:168"],"words":["إني لعملكم من القالين"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Lot may be displaying his aversion to living among them and his wish to escape their bad neighborhood, so he turns from arguing and addresses God.","anchor":"ولعله عليه السلام أراد إظهارالكراهة في مساكنتهم والرغبة في الخلاص من سوء جوارهم ولذلك أعرض عن محاورتهم وتوجه إلى الله قائلا.","mentions":[]}]}
